{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfiyafv3ELvA8eYVhkEGA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Understood. I'm not committing to the library or building any library-specific work. That work stays conditional and unscheduled.\n\n## Committed scope (independent of the library)\n1. **Thumbnail cache and load queue.**\n   - It has a fixed byte budget, LRU eviction, key-based dedupe, and the `Loading`, `Ready`, and `Failed(reason)` states.\n   - It is tested against a fake decoder.\n   - Checks: host-side unit tests for eviction under the cap, dedupe, `Failed` not being retried automatically, and no growth past the budget.\n2. **A `ThumbDecoder` trait boundary.**\n   - The trait is as sketched earlier. Only a fake implementation is built now, and nothing in the design names the library.\n   - The fake covers success, corrupt data, `TooLarge`, and `Unsupported`, so the failure paths are exercised without the library.\n\n## Conditional (not pursued, not scheduled)\nWork in this group needs facts about the library that I can't verify. It starts only if someone supplies those facts and chooses to adopt the library.\n- **A real `ThumbDecoder` implementation.**\n  - It needs the library's supported formats, its `no_std` and `alloc` requirements, and whether it takes caller-supplied buffers.\n  - It also needs to know whether the library can decode at reduced size, and the cap enforcement depends on that. Without reduced-size decode, the decode peak can exceed the budget unless there is a header-size pre-check.\n- **The user-facing list of supported formats.**\n- **Wiring the contracts to a real decode.**\n  - The end-to-end path with a real decode is conditional.\n  - The settled source and rendering contracts are not in this directory, so binding them to the cache is also blocked on their text, not only on the library.\n- **The `max_edge` and cache budget values.** I can't set them without the rendering contract. Treat them as parameters until it's available.\n\nI haven't recommended replacing the library either, because that would be another decision made without evidence.\n\n## Blockers\n- The source and rendering contract text.\n- Whether the target has a global allocator. If not, the cache design changes to caller-provided fixed buffers, and committed item 1 would need rework.\n\nI ran no checks, since no code exists yet."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2629,"cache_read_input_tokens":26998,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2629},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b63f1be-3941-46b0-86fa-8f0e3604cf17","uuid":"0442c508-54e3-4fd0-a4f1-a8bb5f67d133","timestamp":"2026-10-05T11:01:53.725Z","request_id":"req_011Cfiyafdv7J5iHUDVM5td8"}
